--- body ---
## Context — observed facts, one session (aedist, 2026-06-12)

An orchestrator session gating hunt MRs hand-rolled the "chore-close
dance" (close a ticket whose PR merged without erg-pr-merge) three
times. Sequence each time: erg close ID REASON → git mv to closed/ →
chore branch off origin/main → commit → push → PR "Ticket: none" →
auto-merge. Two of three runs stumbled:

1. PR #1008 (aedist): `erg close && git mv && git commit` produced a
   commit with the RENAME but without the `Closed:` header edit —
   git mv staged the pre-edit blob; the header sat unstaged. Caught by
   post-commit inspection (rename 100%, 0 insertions), fixed by
   amend + force-push.
2. Ticket 0551: a chore-close was attempted for a ticket the hunt had
   already closed in a LATE review round (round 2, after the
   orchestrator's earlier file-list snapshot showed no close in the
   PR). erg bounced "no ticket found"; no damage, wasted a cycle.
3. PR #1012 (the run that went clean) only succeeded because the
   operator added an explicit `git add` after erg close — a step not
   documented anywhere.

Adjacent known facts already in memory/rules: `gh pr merge --auto`
bypasses erg close entirely (aedist 0527, closed via fix-up PR #989);
erg-pr-merge cannot be used when the ticket close already rides in the
PR (bounces "no ticket found" on retry) or when the PR branch is held
by another session's worktree.

## Why filed

The dance is now the FOURTH distinct ticket-close path (erg-pr-merge,
in-branch close + plain merge, auto-merge + chore-close, hand dance),
each with its own failure mode. Whether the right move is a helper
script, an erg-pr-merge mode, a documented recipe, or fewer paths is
an Imagine-step decision — deliberately not prescribed here.

## Imagine outcome (2026-07-11)

Wontfix as machinery. Three read-only passes over this repo's history
show the dance is rare and its failure modes already contained:

- All 86 close-and-archive commits in ~310 merged PRs went through
  erg-pr-merge normally; a genuine hand-rolled chore-close is roughly
  1 in 150+ merges. The volume does not justify a helper script or a
  new erg-pr-merge mode.
- The double-close bounce ("no ticket found" on retry) is
  self-correcting: it signals a later review round already closed the
  ticket, and the recovery is to skip.
- The archive-skip failure already has a healthcheck detector.

The one undocumented step — `git add -u tickets/` after `erg close`,
before `git mv`/commit, so the `Closed:` header is not dropped — is now
recorded as a bullet in `rules/git.md` beside the merge-bounce recovery
recipe. No new machinery; the recipe is the deliverable.

## Exit criteria

- [x] Imagine step run on these facts; outcome recorded (even wontfix)
